course: dictionary
lesson: 10933
title: A voyage is a long journey
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A voyage is a long journey, most often by sea, but it can also be a journey in space. Look at the words around it to check. «Admiral Zheng He led seven great voyages from 1405 to 1433» tells you the voyages were long trips, led by a leader over many years, with ships.
explain: Test your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «Charles Darwin filled notebooks on his round-the-world voyage on the ship Beagle» still makes sense if you swap in "long journey": a long journey around the world on the ship Beagle. So your meaning fits.
explain: Voyage can also be a verb, an action word. «The sailors will voyage across the ocean» means they will travel a long way, usually by ship. The word looks the same, but the job it does in the sentence tells you which meaning to use.
fact: A voyage is a long journey, especially by sea or in space.
fact: To voyage is to travel a long way, usually by ship.
fact: «A maiden voyage» means the first trip of a new ship.
fact: «Go on a voyage» and «a sea voyage» are common phrases.
fact: «Admiral Zheng He led seven great voyages from 1405 to 1433» shows that voyages can be planned trips with hundreds of ships.
exercise: «Explorers made great voyages across the oceans.» What is a voyage here? | A short walk in the park | A kind of sea bird | A small boat for fishing | *A long journey, usually by sea
exercise: What is a maiden voyage? | A sailor who cannot swim | A ship that has no sails | The last trip before a ship is sold | *The first trip of a new ship
exercise: Find the word that means to travel a long way by ship: «The crew will voyage across the Pacific next spring.» | Pacific | crew | *voyage | spring
test: «Admiral Zheng He led seven great voyages from 1405 to 1433.» What does voyages mean here? | *Long journeys, especially by sea | Quick trips to the shops | A type of food | Paintings of ships
test: Which sentence uses voyage as a verb, an action word? | The voyage was long, and the food ran low. | *The sailors will voyage to the far islands. | We went on a voyage to the seaside. | The ship's voyage took three months.
exam: In «Charles Darwin filled notebooks on his round-the-world voyage on the ship Beagle», what is a voyage? | A kind of sail | A sailor's song | A pet parrot | *A long journey, usually by sea
